  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe integer $11$ \n{{field-1}}\na multiplicative inverse modulo $35$ since {{field-2}}{{field-3}}.",
  "worked_solution": "An integer $a$ has the multiplicative inverse modulo $n$ if and only if $a$ and $n$ are coprime, i.e., $\\text{gcd}(a,n)=1.$\n\nIn our case, $a=11$ and $n=35.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(11,35)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude the following:\n\nThe integer $11$ $\\text{has}$ the multiplicative inverse modulo $35$ since $\\text{gcd}(11,35)$ $=1.$",
